			"notes": "# RTHuds 6.0.0\n\n## New\n- **Effects HUD**: shows your active effects with icon, name, duration and a duration bar.\n  - Horizontal or vertical layout, with sorting options.\n  - Filters for beneficial, harmful and ambient (beacon) effects.\n  - Option to hide the vanilla effect display.\n  - Dynamic color: the duration text turns yellow, orange and red as time runs out.\n- **Menu themes**: Dark (default), Light, Glass, Frosted glass, Liquid glass, Midnight, Ocean, Forest, Sunset and AMOLED.\n- **RGBA background color** for every HUD.\n- **Turkish translation** (`tr_tr`). All menu and HUD text now lives in the language files.\n\n## Armor HUD\n- Reworked hotbar snapping: once snapped, the HUD stays in place. Click and drag it again to detach.\n- When snapped to the hotbar with the off-hand slot enabled, the vanilla off-hand slot is hidden.\n- Durability text no longer overlaps. Spacing adapts to text length and scale.\n- Added a background panel that wraps icons and text.\n- Added a \"Show empty slots\" option.\n- The durability bar is hidden when the item is at full durability.\n- Added dynamic color: durability text turns yellow, orange and red as durability drops.\n- Added low-durability warning sounds with an adjustable threshold (default 20%): Pling, Bell, Bass, Item break, Anvil or XP orb.\n- Added Chroma support for the text color.\n- The item count is now drawn in the bottom-right corner of the item, like vanilla.\n- The hotbar background now uses the real vanilla hotbar texture.\n\n## HUD Editor\n- Each HUD has a label with its name, `-` / `+` scale buttons and a settings button. Each click changes the scale by 0.1 (range 0.5 to 3.0).\n- Fixed precise dragging with Shift.\n- Armor HUD and Effects HUD align and snap to other HUDs.\n- Shows real items when a player is available, and empty slots otherwise.\n- Default Info HUD positions are now spread over two columns. Your saved positions are unchanged, so press **Reset** to use the new layout.\n\n## Settings\n- Rewrote all settings screens: they fit any resolution and GUI scale, and scroll when needed.\n- Every HUD settings screen has a live preview on the right.\n- Added a per-HUD reset button on the main settings screen.\n- Chroma now shows live in the color preview square.\n\n## Technical\n- Removed the YACL dependency. It is no longer required.\n- Fixed compilation across all supported versions (1.21.1 to 26.3).\n- Fixed the click counter (CPS) mixin target method on 1.21.8 and older."
		},
